Portability patch for libstdc++ (GCC), which the Linux CI build uses.

std::rel_ops lives in <utility>. libc++ happens to make the namespace
visible through <algorithm>, so the macOS build never noticed; libstdc++
does not, and rejects the using-directive outright:

    error: 'rel_ops' is not a namespace-name

Both files use it for the comparison operators their == and < give them.
Adding the include they always needed is the whole change.

--- a/oactobjs32/piadata/DisInsCodeArray.cpp	2026-08-23 09:22:42
+++ b/oactobjs32/piadata/DisInsCodeArray.cpp	2026-08-23 09:22:42
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 // $Id: DisInsCodeArray.cpp 1.23 2017/08/29 09:01:43EDT 277133 Development  $
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <utility>
 #include "DisInsCodeArray.h"
 
 using namespace std;
--- a/oactobjs32/piadata/InsCodeArray.cpp	2026-08-23 09:22:42
+++ b/oactobjs32/piadata/InsCodeArray.cpp	2026-08-23 09:22:42
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
